' Question: which thread does what, and where is the alert safe if the process dies?
' Explained by: ../06-runtime.md. Drawn by hand; the steps are cited there and in ../05-building-blocks.md.
@startuml 06-halt-to-discord
participant "Bot runner\n(bot's thread)" as R
participant BotAlertSource as S
participant AlertHub as H
participant SqliteOutbox as O
participant "Lane\nalerting-lane-discord" as L
participant DiscordWebhookChannel as D
participant ISecretStore as K
participant Discord as X

R -> S : BotChangedEvent(bot_id)
S -> S : GetBotStatusReportQuery(bot_id):\nstate HALTED, was RUNNING
S -> H : publish(Alert BOT_HALTED, CRITICAL)
H -> O : enqueue alert and one PENDING delivery\n(one transaction)
H --> L : nudge
note over R, H : the bot's thread returns here, nothing below can hold it
L -> O : due(discord)
L -> D : deliver(alert, LOUD)
D -> K : read("alerting_discord_webhook")
D -> X : POST
X --> D : 429, retry_after 2 s
D --> L : retry_later(2 s, "rate limited")
L -> O : mark RETRYING, next attempt now + 2 s
note over L : the channel is paused, no request before 2 s
L -> D : deliver(alert, LOUD)
D -> X : POST
X --> D : 204
L -> O : mark SENT
@enduml
